---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
// Works whether or not BASE_URL ends with a slash
const photoSrc = `/images/anjelica.jpeg`;
---

<Layout title="About — Anjelica Martinez" sidebar={true}>
  <div class="about-page">
    <h1>About Me</h1>

    <div class="about-content">
      <div class="intro">
        <img
          src={photoSrc}
          alt="Portrait of Anjelica Martinez"
          class="profile-photo"
          width="220"
          height="220"
          loading="eager"
        />
        <p>
          Hi! I'm Anjelica Martinez, an M.S. candidate in Data Analytics and
          Computational Social Science at UMass Amherst, with a B.A. in
          Psychology from San Jose State. I use statistical modeling and data
          analysis to understand health and behavior, and I'm a native
          Spanish speaker based in Canton, Mississippi.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>
        My background is in psychology research. I ran memory experiments at
        SJSU's Carr Lab, helped collect Twitter data on tic disorders, and am a
        co-author on a hippocampal MRI protocol paper in <em>Hippocampus</em>.
        Before grad school I ran my own photography businesses for years, and
        I still volunteer as a photographer and fundraiser for animal rescues.
      </p>

      <h2>What I Care About</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Behavioral and mental health</li>
        <li>Maternal and child health</li>
        <li>Public health, and health access for Spanish-speaking communities</li>
        <li>Animal welfare and shelter outcomes</li>
        <li>Gaming, music, and how they connect to stress and well-being</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What I'm Working On</h2>
      <p>
        I'm finishing my master's (expected December 2026) and building a
        portfolio of projects that reflect those interests, from childhood
        asthma and low birth weight to music and mental health, repeat visits
        at an animal shelter, and moral language in gaming debates.
      </p>

      <h2>Skills & Tools</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Working knowledge:</strong> R (tidyverse, ggplot2), Python
        (pandas), data cleaning and exploratory analysis, data visualization,
        linear regression, survey design (Qualtrics), RMarkdown, and Jupyter.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Familiar with:</strong> SQL, logistic and ordered logistic
        regression, causal inference (DAGs), time-series and longitudinal
        analysis, NLP and text analysis, machine learning, Bayesian and
        network analysis, Git, and PsychoPy. Currently learning Tableau and
        Power BI.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Languages:</strong> English and Spanish (native, bilingual).
      </p>

      <h2>Get in Touch</h2>
      <p>
        I'm always open to connecting! You can find me on
        <a href="https://github.com/anjelicam" target="_blank">GitHub</a> and
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/anjelicamartinez" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>,
        or reach me by email at
        <a href="mailto:anjelicam@gmail.com">anjelicam@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    padding-top: 1rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  /* Photo + first paragraph side by side */
  .intro {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .profile-photo {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 220px;
    height: 220px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
  }

  /* Stack photo above text on small screens */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .intro {
      flex-direction: column;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .profile-photo {
      width: 160px;
      height: 160px;
    }
  }

  .about-content p {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .about-content .intro p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .about-content ul {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .about-content h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .about-content a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .about-content a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-hover);
  }
</style>